Description: pvr: allow 8 bound descriptor sets
 maxBoundDescriptorSets is a literal 4, equal to PVR_MAX_DESCRIPTOR_SETS.
 The constant sizes the bound sets in struct pvr_descriptor_state
 (pvr_common.h) and the per-set data in pco_common_data (pco_data.h). The PDS
 descriptor program takes up to 8 sets (descriptor_sets[8] in struct
 pvr_pds_descriptor_program_input, pvr_pds.h, and PVR_PDS_MAX_DESC_UPLOAD_BYTES
 counts 8). With 8 sets with dynamic buffers and all special buffers a stage
 needs at most 19 of the PVR_PDS_MAX_BUFFERS (24) entries and 27 DMAs, so
 the constant offsets stay below 256 (const_offset is uint8_t in the const
 map entries) and the 81 data dwords fit the 6-bit pds_data_size fields of
 VDMCTRL_PDS_STATE0 and CDMCTRL_KERNEL0 (16-byte units, vdm.xml, cdm.xml).
 .
 Raise the constant to 8 and report it; the Vulkan 1.4 minimum is 7. With 6
 or more sets zink leaves its compact descriptor mode and uses one set per
 descriptor type (zink_screen.c).
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
